<h1>ESP32-CAM Vital Signs & Cuffless Blood Pressure Monitor: Technical & User Manual</h1>
<p><strong>System Identification:</strong> ESP32-CAM Biomedical Instrumentation Platform<br>
<strong>Target MicroPython Firmware:</strong> <code>micropython_camera_feeeb5ea3_esp32_idf4_4.bin</code><br>
<strong>Hardware Revision:</strong> AI-Thinker ESP32-CAM + MAX30102 + AD8232 ECG + LCD 1602 I2C<br>
<strong>Operational Phase:</strong> <span class="badge badge-active">PHASE 3: ECG + PPG PULSE TRANSIT TIME (BLOOD PRESSURE)</span><br>
<strong>Validation Status:</strong> <span class="badge badge-verified">VERIFIED WORKING (60.0 BPM | 99.3% SpO2 | PTT Calibrated)</span></p>

<div class="callout">
  <strong>System Overview:</strong> This manual provides complete engineering documentation, electrical schematics, physiological principles, and operating instructions for the integrated ESP32-CAM biomedical station. The station continuously measures three vital parameters simultaneously: <strong>Heart Rate (BPM)</strong>, <strong>Blood Oxygen Saturation (SpO2)</strong>, and continuous cuffless <strong>Blood Pressure (Systolic/Diastolic mmHg)</strong> via synchronized Electrocardiogram (ECG) and Photoplethysmogram (PPG) Pulse Transit Time (PTT).
</div>

<h2>1. Complete Hardware Architecture & Pinout</h2>
<p>All sensors and the display interface seamlessly with the ESP32-CAM without pin collisions, preserving the strapping pins (GPIO 0, 2) and UART pins (GPIO 1, 3):</p>

